From: ScorchDroid <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: give the host its own copy of a drawn plan line

ServerLinesHandler is where a client's ComsLinesMessage arrives and is
relayed to the sender's team. On a desktop the host is a separate process
with no map of its own, so upstream has no reason to keep a copy; here the
host is a player, and without this the person hosting is the one player who
cannot see what anyone else draws.

It has to be a call inside this handler rather than a second handler
registered for the type: ComsMessageHandler keeps exactly one handler per
message id (`recvHandlers_[id] = handler`), so registering would replace this
relay outright and nobody would receive anything.

Placed after every check the handler makes - the 150-point cap, the
provably-from-that-tank destination test and the mute gate - so a message
that is rejected is as invisible to the host as it is to everyone else. No
game logic; the work is in porting/PlanLineStore.cpp.

---
diff --git a/src/server/server/ServerLinesHandler.cpp b/src/server/server/ServerLinesHandler.cpp
index 86e75427..b059bf4c 100644
--- a/src/server/server/ServerLinesHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/server/server/ServerLinesHandler.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,12 @@
 #include <tank/TankState.hpp>
 #include <common/Logger.hpp>
 #include <set>
+// Android build: the host's own copy of a line a client drew. There is no
+// socket to yourself and so no client-side handler to run, and a second
+// handler cannot simply be registered for the type - ComsMessageHandler keeps
+// one per message id, so registering would replace this relay rather than sit
+// beside it. See PlanLineStore.h and the porting plan.
+#include <PlanLineStore.h>
 
 ServerLinesHandler::ServerLinesHandler(ComsMessageHandler &comsMessageHandler)
 {
@@ -63,6 +69,21 @@ bool ServerLinesHandler::processMessage(
 	// If this tank has been muted also don't allow lines
 	if (tank->getState().getMuted()) return true;
 
+	// Android build: the host is a player too, and every check that decides
+	// whether this message is allowed at all has just passed. Placed here
+	// rather than at the top so a rejected message is as invisible to the
+	// host as it is to everyone else.
+	{
+		std::vector<float> points;
+		points.reserve(message.getLines().size() * 2);
+		for (Vector &point : message.getLines())
+		{
+			points.push_back(point[0]);
+			points.push_back(point[1]);
+		}
+		ScorchDroidPlanLines::pushStroke(playerId, points);
+	}
+
 	// Get destinationinfo for this tank
 	ServerDestination *destinationInfo =
 		ScorchedServer::instance()->getServerDestinations().getDestination(netMessage.getDestinationId());
